      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Method"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "orderedList",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Blend the canned tomatoes, red pepper, chilli and the roughly chopped onion until smooth."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Heat the oil in a large heavy-bottomed saucepan over medium-high heat. Fry the sliced onion for 5 minutes until softened."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Add the garlic and fry for 1 minute. Add the tomato puree and cook, stirring, for 2 minutes."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Pour in the blended tomato mixture. Add bay leaves, thyme, smoked paprika and salt. Cook uncovered over medium heat for 20 minutes, stirring occasionally, until the sauce darkens and the oil floats to the surface."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Add the rinsed rice and stir to coat in the sauce. Add 400ml water. Stir once, bring to a boil, then reduce to the lowest heat."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Cover tightly with foil and then a lid. Cook for 25 minutes without lifting the lid."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Remove the lid and foil. Increase heat to high for 3 to 5 minutes to develop the smoky base. Remove from heat, replace the lid and rest for 5 minutes before serving."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "troubleshooter",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "troubleshooterItem",
            "attrs": {
              "symptom": "Rice is mushy",
              "cause": "Too much water or lid lifted during cooking",
              "fix": "Use a 1:1 ratio of rice to blended tomato plus water. Do not lift the lid until the timer is up."
            }
          },
          {
            "type": "troubleshooterItem",
            "attrs": {
              "symptom": "Rice is still hard inside",
              "cause": "Heat too low or insufficient water",
              "fix": "Add 3 tablespoons of water, replace foil and lid, and cook on low for another 10 minutes."
            }
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Where this dish lives"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Jollof rice appears across West Africa under different names and with fierce regional loyalty. Nigeria's version tends to be heavily spiced and cooked on very high heat. Ghana's version is typically lighter and often served with fried plantain. It is the centrepiece of celebrations from Lagos to Accra and has become one of the most recognised dishes of the African continent."
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  }
}